{"_links":{"self":{"href":"/api/v2/versions/288011"},"stash:dataset":{"href":"/api/v2/datasets/doi%3A10.5061%2Fdryad.2v6wwpzt3"},"stash:files":{"href":"/api/v2/versions/288011/files"},"stash:download":{"href":"/api/v2/versions/288011/download"},"curies":[{"name":"stash","href":"https://github.com/datadryad/dryad-app/blob/main/documentation/apis/link_relations.md#{rel}","templated":"true"}]},"title":"Release of cognitive and multimodal MRI data including real-world tasks and hippocampal subfield segmentations ","authors":[{"firstName":"Ian A.","lastName":"Clark","email":"","affiliation":"University College London","affiliationROR":"https://ror.org/02jx3x895","affiliations":[{"organization":"University College London","identifier":"https://ror.org/02jx3x895"}],"orcid":null,"order":0,"roles":[]},{"firstName":"Eleanor A.","lastName":"Maguire","email":"e.maguire@ucl.ac.uk","affiliation":"University College London","affiliationROR":"https://ror.org/02jx3x895","affiliations":[{"organization":"University College London","identifier":"https://ror.org/02jx3x895"}],"orcid":"0000-0002-9470-6324","order":1,"roles":[]}],"abstract":"\u003cp\u003eWe share data from N=217 healthy adults (mean age: 29 years, range 20–41; 109 females, 108 males) who underwent extensive cognitive assessment and neuroimaging to examine the neural basis of individual differences, with a particular focus on a brain structure called the hippocampus. Cognitive data were collected using a wide array of questionnaires, naturalistic tests that examined imagination, autobiographical memory recall and spatial navigation, traditional laboratory-based tests such as recalling word pairs, and comprehensive characterisation of the strategies used to perform the cognitive tests. 3 Tesla MRI data were also acquired and include multi-parameter mapping to examine tissue microstructure, diffusion-weighted MRI, T2-weighted high-resolution partial volume structural MRI scans (with the masks of hippocampal subfields manually segmented from these scans), whole brain resting state functional MRI scans and partial volume high-resolution resting-state functional MRI scans. This rich dataset will be of value to cognitive and clinical neuroscientists researching individual differences, real-world cognition, brain-behaviour associations, hippocampal subfields and more. \u003c/p\u003e","funders":[{"organization":"Wellcome Trust","identifierType":"ror","identifier":"https://ror.org/029chgv08","awardNumber":"101759/Z/13/Z","awardURI":null,"awardDescription":null,"awardTitle":null,"order":null},{"organization":"Wellcome Trust","identifierType":"ror","identifier":"https://ror.org/029chgv08","awardNumber":"210567/Z/18/Z","awardURI":null,"awardDescription":null,"awardTitle":null,"order":null},{"organization":"Wellcome Trust","identifierType":"ror","identifier":"https://ror.org/029chgv08","awardNumber":"203147/Z/16/Z","awardURI":null,"awardDescription":null,"awardTitle":null,"order":null}],"keywords":["individual differences","Hippocampus","real world","naturalistic","Memory","MRI","Cognition","subfields","Navigation","autobiographical memory","imagination","future thinking"],"fieldOfScience":"Biological sciences","relatedWorks":[{"relationship":"article","identifierType":"DOI","identifier":"https://doi.org/10.1037/xge0000582"},{"relationship":"article","identifierType":"DOI","identifier":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cognition.2019.104114"},{"relationship":"article","identifierType":"DOI","identifier":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.neuroimage.2020.117211"},{"relationship":"article","identifierType":"DOI","identifier":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyg.2020.02119"},{"relationship":"article","identifierType":"DOI","identifier":"https://doi.org/10.1177/23982128211011923"},{"relationship":"article","identifierType":"DOI","identifier":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fnins.2021.706473"},{"relationship":"article","identifierType":"DOI","identifier":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.mri.2022.07.002"},{"relationship":"article","iden